          "verify": "Run `python main.py` again. Open output.csv: (1) every existing row still has its original values in the old columns - you didn't break anything; (2) your new column has a real value on the document(s) where it applies; (3) run it specifically against sample_data/product_review.txt - your new column for that row must come back blank, since a coffee-maker review has no job title, company name, or address to honestly report.",
          "instruction": "Add ONE new field to the FIELDS dict in extractor.py - pick something that appears in at least one sample file but not all of them (a job title, a company name, a listing location). Write your own one-line description for it, the same style as the existing five:"
